<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aedemon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aedemon was a freedman of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemy-of-mauretania">Ptolemy of Mauretania</a> who led a revolt after the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caligula">Caligula</a> had Ptolemy executed in 40 CE. Roman forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaius-suetonius-paulinus">Suetonius Paulinus</a> and Hosidius Geta put down the rising in 41–42 CE, after which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claudius">Claudius</a> annexed the kingdom and divided it into the provinces of Mauretania Tingitana and Mauretania Caesariensis.</p></div>
